+Vehicles that do not report paddle events will not respond. Modes 1–3 use the same behavior for both paddles.
+
+Mode 4 requires openpilot longitudinal control and support for four gap levels. With Drive selected and valid CAN/control input, a new press during normal cruise ON changes one step; release and holding do not add steps. Stock regen adjustments during standby, disengagement, CANCEL or independent SoftHold do not change the saved gap; re-engagement keeps that gap. A paddle held from OFF must be released and pressed again after ON to change the gap. Entering or leaving mode 4 requires a control-process restart. CANCEL, pedal and parking protection remain in effect, and a paddle press does not engage cruise. Vehicle validation is still required.
+
+A gap request already accepted during normal ON may finish saving after disengagement if storage is delayed. The direct gap button and web setting remain usable while disengaged.
+
+On MQ4 HEV CANFD camera-SCC with openpilot longitudinal control, a new gesture during normal ACC in the applied mode 4 keeps the ACC request continuous. A valid release of both paddles must be observed after startup. CANCEL, pedal input or invalid input/control revokes the exception until a new full release. Normal ACC stop/restart is included; independent SoftHold and CarrotCruise are excluded. Other vehicles and modes 0–3 retain their existing policy. Stock regen signals are not masked; regen-state preservation after cruise cancellation and long holds require vehicle validation.
 
